use flake .

# `use flake .` keys its cache on flake.nix/flake.lock only, so editing what
# they import regenerates nothing: a stale devshell keeps being served and a
# package added to modules/ appears to have no effect at all. That is exactly
# how `python3` went missing from `just switch`'s PATH after being added to
# modules/infra/devshell.nix — a new terminal loaded the old profile, and only
# `direnv reload` fixed it.
#
# The devshell definition is the file worth watching: it is where packages are
# added, and it is the one import-tree input whose edits are meant to change
# this environment. Feature modules under modules/features/ do not affect the
# shell's package set.
watch_file modules/infra/devshell.nix
